      "extract": "[]{#section2.1 label=\"section2.1\"} ::: defn []{#height1 label=\"height1\"} 1. Let $n\\ge k$, $\\nu\\vdash k$, and $\\eta\\vdash n$. We shall assume that $n\\ge 2k+2$. Assume $\\nu \\le\\eta$ and that $S$ is a part of the rim of $\\eta$ such that $\\eta\\setminus S=\\nu$, then we write $\\eta=\\nu*S$. Let $h(S)$ denote the height of $S$. . Given such $\\eta=\\nu*S$, we say that \\\"$S$ covers $\\nu$\\\" if $\\nu'_1\\le h(S)$. Otherwise $S$",
