      "extract": "Our aim is to prove the following formula. ::: thm []{#v4 label=\"v4\"} Let $\\nu=(\\nu_1,\\nu_2,\\ldots )\\vdash k$, $n\\ge 2k+2$ . Let $\\mu=(\\mu_1,\\mu_2,\\ldots )\\vdash n$, and denote $\\bar\\mu=(\\mu_2,\\mu_3,\\ldots)$, so $\\mu_1=n-k$ if and only if $\\bar\\mu\\vdash k$. Then $$\\begin{aligned} \\label{general.conjecture} \\psi_{\\nu,n}(\\mu)=\\begin{cases}\\chi^\\nu(\\bar\\mu)\\cdot(n-k) & if ~\\mu_1= n-k \\\\ 0 & if ~\\mu_1\\ne n-k\\\\",
      "extractCut": true
